  "stages": [
    {
      "part_no": 1,
      "function_en": "Introduction",
      "function_zh": "引言：破題與定義",
      "language_pattern": "rhetorical questions / X is about ...",
      "source_description": "Micro-Hook: Global context of technology",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 1,
          "title": {
            "en": "Micro-Hook: Global context of technology",
            "zh": "全球永續連結"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Good morning. Today we look at SDG 9, a global plan from the United Nations. It asks every country to back new technology and to build stronger systems.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 5.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Good morning. SDG 9 has one central aim: it asks governments everywhere to fund modern research and to build the kind of strong networks that a scientific nation depends on.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 7.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Good morning. The ninth Sustainable Development Goal is a global framework that commits every country to backing new technology and to building the networks on which our future science depends.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 10.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 2,
          "title": {
            "en": "AI as Innovation: Connecting SDG 9",
            "zh": "科技與創新"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "AI is changing how we study and how we do our research today. It gets better every year. So one question stays with us: what makes people special?",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 4.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Artificial intelligence has changed the way we study, the way we run tests and the way we build new tools. As it becomes more capable, one question keeps returning. What makes us irreplaceable?",
              "words": 33,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 11.0,
              "fk_grade": 7.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 18.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Artificial intelligence is transforming how we study, how we conduct research and how we develop new technology. As it grows more capable, one question becomes unavoidable: what makes a human irreplaceable?",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 14.1,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 2,
      "function_en": "Problem",
      "function_zh": "問題指認：趨勢與因果",
      "language_pattern": "present progressive for trends / this causes ...",
      "source_description": "Student Experience",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 3,
          "title": {
            "en": "Student Experience",
            "zh": "學生生活情境"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Many science students feel excited. But they also feel a bit afraid. These tools write our lab reports, sum up short articles and make computer code in seconds.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 4.9,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Science undergraduates are excited by these tools. They are also nervous, and I understand why. A system that writes a lab report, summarises an article and produces working code in seconds is hard to match.",
              "words": 35,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 11.7,
              "fk_grade": 8.2,
              "speak_seconds_est": 19.1,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Science majors are enthusiastic about these systems and anxious about them at the same time. Code produced in seconds, summaries of journal articles and finished laboratory reports now arrive without any effort at all.",
              "words": 34,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 17.0,
              "fk_grade": 12.2,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 4,
          "title": {
            "en": "Contextualized Problem",
            "zh": "脈絡化問題"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "The worry makes sense, because machines now do jobs that once needed people. But speed is not the same as science. A fast answer is not real understanding.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 4.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "The nerves are understandable, because machines now handle work that used to need a person. Yet finishing a task fast is not the same as understanding it, and science needs the second.",
              "words": 32,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.0,
              "fk_grade": 8.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "The anxiety is reasonable, although it rests on a confusion. A system that completes a task efficiently has understood nothing, and understanding is the part that science is actually made of.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 10.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 3,
      "function_en": "Achievements",
      "function_zh": "成果：舉證與比較",
      "language_pattern": "present perfect / comparatives",
      "source_description": "Scientific Explanation",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 5,
          "title": {
            "en": "Scientific Explanation",
            "zh": "解釋科學原理 WHY"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Why? A model can spot patterns in a huge pile of data, but it never understands them. It picks each word from the odds, and never from curiosity.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 4.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "A model can find patterns in enormous amounts of data, but it has no real grasp of what any of those patterns mean. It weighs probabilities instead of asking questions.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 8.0,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "The mechanism explains the limit. Because a model is trained to predict the next likely word, its fluency reflects a regularity in old text rather than reasoning, curiosity or judgment.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 11.1,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 6,
          "title": {
            "en": "Scientific Explanation",
            "zh": "解釋科學原理 HOW"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "People work in another way. We ask new questions, plan clever tests, and study odd results. We learn from our own errors, and that takes real imagination.",
              "words": 27,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.0,
              "fk_grade": 5.4,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.1,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Human researchers behave in a different way. We invent questions nobody has asked before, we design new tests, we puzzle over odd results and we learn from failure. Real discovery still runs on imagination.",
              "words": 34,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 11.3,
              "fk_grade": 9.0,
              "speak_seconds_est": 18.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Human researchers move another way, asking fresh questions, designing tests that may fail, reading results nobody saw coming and learning from every failure. Discovery has always depended on imagination and patience.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 13.3,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 4,
      "function_en": "Solutions",
      "function_zh": "解方：做法與取捨",
      "language_pattern": "instead of + V-ing / modal verbs",
      "source_description": "Impact on Science",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 7,
          "title": {
            "en": "Impact on Science",
            "zh": "學術研究衝擊"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Every big discovery in history started with a curious person. AI can sort old facts very well. But it cannot choose which new question is worth our time.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 5.3,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "History is clear about this. Every major breakthrough has begun with somebody who was curious, and although AI can organise what we already know, it cannot decide which question is worth asking.",
              "words": 32,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.0,
              "fk_grade": 10.2,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "History settles the argument. Every breakthrough has started with a person who was curious, and while a model can process what we already know, it cannot judge which unanswered question is worth investigating.",
              "words": 33,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.5,
              "fk_grade": 11.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 8,
          "title": {
            "en": "Impact on Society",
            "zh": "大眾社會衝擊"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Science is more than a quick result. A scientist must think about safety, about the planet, and about other people. A machine cannot weigh those things.",
              "words": 26,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.7,
              "fk_grade": 5.0,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Science is about more than results. If a discovery threatens public safety, the environment or the people around it, someone has to say so, and no computer rule will ever do that.",
              "words": 32,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.0,
              "fk_grade": 9.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Science is also more than the production of results. Ethical choice, public safety, environmental sustainability and social responsibility are judgments that a human community makes, and no algorithm can be delegated to make them.",
              "words": 34,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 17.0,
              "fk_grade": 15.0,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 5,
      "function_en": "Implications",
      "function_zh": "影響：推論後果",
      "language_pattern": "first conditional / however",
      "source_description": "AI Literacy Strategy 1",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 9,
          "title": {
            "en": "AI Literacy Strategy 1",
            "zh": "AI 素養策略一： 提問前的後設認知"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "So treat AI as a partner, and never as a replacement for your own mind. It can arrange the facts for you. But your choices stay your own.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 2.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Treat AI as a partner in the work, not as a substitute for thinking. It can organise information and save you hours, but the final judgement must still be yours.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 6.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Treat the system as a collaborator rather than a replacement. It can organise material and raise your efficiency, yet the decision about what actually matters has to stay with the person who signs the paper.",
              "words": 35,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 17.5,
              "fk_grade": 11.1,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 10,
          "title": {
            "en": "AI Literacy Strategy 2",
            "zh": "AI 素養策略二： 具體動作"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "As future scientists, we must keep asking good questions. We must doubt old ideas, and we must share what we find. Those human skills will always matter.",
              "words": 27,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.0,
              "fk_grade": 3.2,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.1,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "As future scientists, we have to keep asking awkward questions, testing old ideas and sharing our results in an honest way. Those human habits will matter however clever the software gets.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 8.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.9,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "As future scientists, we should keep asking uncomfortable questions, testing old ideas and reporting our results with honesty. Those human habits stay essential, however advanced the machine in front of us becomes.",
              "words": 32,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.0,
              "fk_grade": 12.0,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 6,
      "function_en": "Call to action",
      "function_zh": "結語：總結與號召",
      "language_pattern": "to wrap up ... / let's ...",
      "source_description": "The Human Edge: Redefining the human role",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 11,
          "title": {
            "en": "The Human Edge: Redefining the human role",
            "zh": "人類獨特價值"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "SDG 9 reminds us that people drive every new idea. A machine can hand us facts. But only a person can turn facts into real knowledge.",
              "words": 26,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.7,
              "fk_grade": 4.1,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "SDG 9 reminds us that new ideas are driven by people. A machine can generate information, but only human beings turn that information into knowledge that somebody can act on.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 9.9,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "SDG 9 reminds us that innovation is driven by people. A machine generates information, whereas only human beings convert information into knowledge, ethical decisions and change that actually means something.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 13.9,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 12,
          "title": {
            "en": "Final Call to Action: The SDG 9 future vision",
            "zh": "最終呼籲與願景"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "So let's use AI wisely. Keep your wonder, your new ideas and your honest heart. Those three habits really make a scientist, and they build a better future.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 4.1,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "So let's use AI wisely while we go on developing the curiosity, the creativity and the sense of responsibility that great scientists share. That is how we earn a future worth having.",
              "words": 32,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.0,
              "fk_grade": 9.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "So let's use AI with judgement, and go on cultivating the curiosity, the creativity and the professional responsibility that define a scientist. Only then does the future we build become one worth trusting.",
              "words": 33,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.5,
              "fk_grade": 11.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
